<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tinmel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tinmel is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">High Atlas</a> Mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. In the early twelfth century the religious reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tumart">Ibn Tumart</a> established his base there after proclaiming himself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>, making it the cradle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> movement. Its twelfth-century mosque, built under the Almohads, survives as an important monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tinmel.jpg" alt="Tinmel" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jerzy Strzelecki · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tin_Mal_Mosque1_(js).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
